This blueprint describes the Lean formalization in the [posqmf](https://github.com/seewoo5/posqmf)
repository. It follows three sources, and its chapters are organized accordingly.

* _Positive quasimodular forms and the sign uncertainty principle_
  {Informal.citep lee2026sign}[]. The chapters on Eisenstein series, on Kaneko–Zagier operators,
  on the polynomial model, on the two families of Feigenbaum, Grabner and Hardin, and on the
  logarithm inequalities formalize Lemmas 2.2, 2.3 and 2.4, Proposition 4.9, Propositions 4.22,
  4.23 and 4.24, and the inequalities behind Lemma 4.17 and Theorem 4.18 of that paper, together
  with the parts of Theorem 4.1 and Proposition 4.21 that these rely on. Numbering refers to the
  second arXiv version.
* _Inequalities involving polynomials and quasimodular forms_ {Informal.citep lee2026polymod}[].
  One chapter formalizes the inequalities (41), (60) and (61) of that paper.
* Two results on extremal quasimodular forms beyond the range of the conjecture of Kaneko and
  Koike: that every coefficient of the extremal form $`X_{16,5}` but the first is negative, a claim
  of the author's PhD thesis {Informal.citep lee2026thesis}[], and that the extremal form
  $`\mathcal{D}_{6,3}` of level $`\Gamma_0(2)` is completely positive, from the author's manuscript
  _On extremal quasimodular forms of low levels_. The last chapter proves the second, and the first
  for all coefficients from the $`250`-th on.

